2. Personal and Non-Commercial License

Subject to these terms, White-Lotus grants an individual natural person a
non-exclusive, non-transferable license to download, install, run, inspect, and
privately modify the Software solely for that person's personal,
non-commercial, educational, or evaluation purposes on systems that person is
authorized to use.

Private modifications must remain private. No right to publish, distribute,
sublicense, sell, transfer, or provide the Software or a modified version is
granted, except for the limited Small Developer License in Section 3.

3. Limited Small Developer License

A "Qualifying Small Developer" is an individual or legal entity that, together
with its controlling, controlled, and commonly controlled affiliates:

(a) has no more than five total employees and individual contractors; and

(b) received no more than USD 100,000 in total gross revenue during its most
recently completed fiscal year, or during the preceding twelve months if it has
not completed a fiscal year.

Subject to these terms, White-Lotus grants a Qualifying Small Developer a
non-exclusive, non-transferable license to download, install, run, inspect,
copy internally, build, privately modify, and use the Software in its own
development and DevOps work, including revenue-generating work. This permission
does not include redistribution, resale, sublicensing, hosted-service use, or
product integration prohibited by Sections 5 and 6.

Eligibility is measured across the developer and all affiliates, not per team,
repository, office, or subsidiary. A licensee that ceases to qualify must stop
commercial and organizational use within 30 days unless White-Lotus grants a
separate written license.

4. Other Organizational and Commercial Use Prohibited

Except for a Qualifying Small Developer under Section 3, no corporation,
limited-liability company, partnership, government agency, employer,
commercial organization, or other legal entity may use, copy, reproduce,
modify, build, distribute, sublicense, sell, lease, host, deploy, or otherwise
exploit the Software without prior written permission from White-Lotus.

An individual may not exercise the personal license on behalf of, for the
benefit of, or within the scope of employment or engagement by such an entity.
Internal business use, production use, consulting use, and use in a paid or
revenue-generating activity are commercial uses and are prohibited unless
Section 3 applies or White-Lotus grants a separate written license.

5. Redistribution Prohibited

No licensee may distribute or make available copies of the Software, its source
code, compiled binaries, installer packages, substantial portions, modified
versions, or derivative works to any third party. Linking to a release made
available directly by White-Lotus is permitted, but mirroring or repackaging it
is not.

6. Hosted Services and Product Integration Prohibited

The Software may not be offered as a hosted or managed service, exposed as part
of a software-as-a-service product, embedded in another product, used to provide
services to third parties, or incorporated into a commercial or organizational
workflow without prior written permission from White-Lotus.

7. Machine Learning and Automated Extraction Prohibited

The Software may not be used to train, fine-tune, evaluate, or improve a
commercial artificial-intelligence or machine-learning system, nor collected
into a dataset for those purposes, except to the minimum extent that a hosting
provider's mandatory terms require for hosting the repository.

8. Repository Hosting Rights

If White-Lotus publishes the Software through a source-hosting service, the
limited technical rights necessarily granted to that service and its users by
